    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a78826752f2e2840152f6563b9f01df&id=8a78879ea0f4259701a10da01e185488": {
      "title": "Recording Studio Graduate Assistant",
      "description": "Dominican University Careers Careers JOIN OUR TEAM Position: Recording Studio Graduate Assistant Location: River Forest, IL Job Id: 2409 # of Openings: 1 Position: Recording Studio Graduate Assistant Department: Rebecca Crown Library Reports to: User Experience Librarian Hourly rate: $15.00 Position availability: Academic Year 2026-27 Hours needed per week: 4-8 ITEMS TO INCLUDE IN APPLICATION: Cover Letter & Resume should include class schedule and technology/software familiarity EXPECTATIONS FOR ALL DOMINICAN EMPLOYEES: To support the University's mission of preparing students to pursue truth, to give compassionate service, and to participate in the creation of a more just and humane world. JOB COMPONENTS/PRINCIPAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: Provide individual and group instruction on Recording Studio equipment and skills Learn how these tools work inside and out as you troubleshoot, maintain, and document our Recording Studio equipment Aid with various elements of video production Maintain machines, tools, materials, safe use, and schedule of the Recording Studio Facilitate workshops and training for students on the use of equipment and safety protocols Develop projects in partnership with student organizations and groups interested in promoting use/space of Recording Studio Assist with Recording Studio events, workshops, and classes Perform other duties as requested, delegated or assigned [Student workers will be trained in aspects of job performance duties.] BASIC COMPETENCIES: (Required knowledge, skills, abilities) Ability to deal effectively and efficiently with patrons Good communication skills with patrons and supervisors Dependability and ability to work independently Knowledge of Audacity, Garageband, Panopto, DaVinci Resolve (preferred but not required) Should be familiar with various methods, techniques and materials used in video production Must be enrolled at least at part-time, degree-seeking status at Dominican University Must be eligible for US Employment Apply for this Position Go back to the job list powered by Dominican University | (708) 366-2490"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a78826752f2e2840152f6563b9f01df&id=8a7883a8a184746e01a1a2db20b04f69": {
      "title": "Event Coordinator",
      "description": "Dominican University Careers Careers JOIN OUR TEAM Position: Event Coordinator Location: River Forest, IL Job Id: 2418 # of Openings: 1 JOB TITLE: Event Coordinator DEPARTMENT: Event Services REPORTS TO: Manager of Event Operations and Logistics JOB STATUS: Full Time LOCATION: River Forest Main Campus PRIMARY PURPOSE/ POSITION SUMMARY: The Event Coordinator provides on-site operational and logistical support for Dominican University events and meetings, serving as a key point of coordination for internal and external clients, vendors, catering, Facilities and Maintenance, and other campus partners. The position helps ensure events are properly prepared, safely executed, and professionally supported from setup through completion. The Event Coordinator supports the Event Services mission by translating approved event plans into successful day-of-event operations, managing event technology, supervising event activity and student staff when assigned, and completing required post-event reporting. This position works closely with external vendors, catering, Facilities and Maintenance, Campus Safety, technology/AV partners, and event clients. The role will support both internal University events and external events. This position requires irregular hours, including evenings, nights, and weekends, based on scheduled events and institutional needs. EXPECTATIONS FOR ALL DOMINICAN EMPLOYEES: To support the University's mission of preparing students to pursue truth, to give compassionate service, and to participate in the creation of a more just and humane world. JOB COMPONENTS/PRINCIPAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: Vendor & Support Services Coordination: Coordinate with external vendors, catering, and campus service partners to support approved internal and external events. Verify and communicate operational requirements, including certificates of insurance (COI), parking, loading/unloading, access, and related event needs. Day-of-Event Facilities & Logistics: Prepare event spaces and place event signage; coordinate with catering, maintenance, Facilities, and other campus partners to ensure room setups, equipment, service areas, and related logistical needs are correct, safe, functional, and ready for guests. Event Technology & Hybrid Event Support: Set up, operate, and strike in-room event technology and audiovisual equipment as appropriate to the event. Provide operational support for Zoom meetings, webinars, and other hybrid-event technology when needed. Event Supervision & On-Site Coordination: Supervise the operational execution of assigned events, including installation, event activities, and removal/strike as needed. Monitor event conditions and coordinate timely responses to operational issues during the event. Student Staff Supervision: Provide direction and on-site supervision to student event staff when deployed, including assigning tasks, monitoring performance, and ensuring staff follow event procedures and service expectations. Event Reporting & Reconciliation: Complete post-event reports and provide required event information, including recording links, audience counts, registration wrap-up, and reconciliation information as applicable. Client & Campus Partner Communication: Maintain clear and timely communication with event clients and campus partners regarding day-of-event needs, changes, operational issues, and completion of assigned event responsibilities. Perform other duties as requested, delegated, or assigned. QUALIFICATIONS: All qualifications are required unless otherwise indicated. Bachelor’s degree and relevant experience in event coordination, hospitality, facilities operations, audiovisual support, or related field. Demonstrated ability to coordinate multiple operational tasks and priorities in a fast-paced event environment. Must have the ability to work a flexible schedule, including evenings and weekends, based on event schedules. Ability to safely perform the physical requirements associated with event setup, operation, and strike, including moving event materials and equipment as appropriate. Must be committed to fostering an equitable and inclusive working and learning environment. PREFERRED COMPETENCIES: Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Previous experience coordinating events in a higher education, conference, performing arts, hospitality, or comparable environment. Experience working with catering, facilities, maintenance, vendors, and other service providers in support of events. Working knowledge of Zoom, webinar platforms, presentation technology, and basic audiovisual equipment. Ability to troubleshoot event technology and identify when escalation or additional support is required. Strong organizational, interpersonal, and customer service skills. Ability to prioritize tasks, adapt to changing event conditions, and meet time-sensitive deadlines. Experience supervising or directing student employees or temporary event staff. Familiarity with event registration, attendance tracking, post-event reporting. BENEFITS Comprehensive health, dental, and vision insurance Retirement plan with employer matching contributions Professional development opportunities Tuition remission for employees and their dependents Flexible spending accounts (FSA) Generous paid time off (PTO) Physical Demands: Ability to spend long durations of the workday sitting at a desk and working on a computer Ability to lift up to 15 pounds at times Note: accommodation will be made for applicants who cannot meet these physical demands Salary and FLSA Status Salary: $45,000 - $48,000 FLSA Status: (exempt/salaried, non-exempt/hourly; PT20, PT30, FT) Employment at Dominican University is contingent upon the successful completion of a background investigation. About Dominican University Dominican University is a Catholic, comprehensive teaching university located in River Forest, a suburb of Chicago, with an additional campus in the Pilsen neighborhood of Chicago. Accredited by the Higher Learning Commission, Dominican University offers associate, baccalaureate, master’s, and doctoral degrees. It is highly regarded for its academic rigor, thoughtful accompaniment of students, intentional affordability, and values-based, relationship-centered learning environment. Dominican currently enrolls over 3,800 students, including 2,690 undergraduates and 1,114 graduate students. Sixty-eight percent (68%) of undergraduate students identify as Latinx, 5% as Black or African American, and 3% as Asian. Under-represented minority students comprise 77% of the undergraduate enrollment and 38% of the graduate enrollment. Over 90 percent of undergraduates receive some form of financial aid. Nearly half of all undergraduates are first-generation college students; over half are federal Pell Grant recipients, illustrating their families’ level of income; and 58% are eligible for low-income MAP grants from the State of Illinois. Recognized since 2011 as a Hispanic-Serving Institution (HSI) by the U.S. Department of Education, Dominican is committed to expanding and enhancing educational opportunities for Latinx students and all students from historically underrepresented groups. For more information, visit www.dom.edu. Expectations for all Dominican Employees To support the University's mission of preparing students to pursue truth, give compassionate service, and participate in the creation of a more just and humane world, engage in university service work that promotes collaboration and community building. This includes participating in organizational initiatives, supporting campus events, contributing to community outreach, and fostering a supportive environment through involvement in various staff-driven activities and groups. Institutional Statement Dominican University is committed to fostering a supportive academic community that provides access and opportunity for all our students. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement Dominican University is an equal opportunity employer and complies with all federal and state employment regulations. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by law. If you need accommodations due to a disability, you may contact us at opc@dom.edu for assistance. Apply for this Position Go back to the job list powered by Dominican University | (708) 366-2490"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a78826752f2e2840152f6563b9f01df&id=8a7885a8a184742e01a1a2a0d5404609": {
      "title": "Honors and International Advisor – Part Time 20 Hours",
      "description": "Dominican University Careers Careers JOIN OUR TEAM Position: Honors and International Advisor – Part Time 20 Hours Location: River Forest, IL Job Id: 2416 # of Openings: 1 Job Title: Honors and International Advisor – Part Time 20 Hours Department: Academic Affairs Reports to: Executive Director of Academic Success & University Registrar Partners with: Director of Study Abroad Programs & Director of the Mazzuchelli Honors Program Honors and International Advisor is a critical member of the academic advising team, serving three populations: students in the Mazzuchelli Scholars Honors Program, incoming international students for the F-1 program under Department of Homeland Seccurity, and incoming (J-1 exchange visitors under the Department of State) and outgoing students participating in study abroad programs. The position requires a dynamic and collaborative approach, and the ability to work with colleagues from across the university to support these students. This position will work closely with the Director of the Mazzuchelli Scholars Honors Program to provide academic and programmatic advising support to Mazzuchelli Scholars. Serving as a Designated School Official (DSO) and Alternate Responsible Officer (ARO), this position leads all aspects of F-1 and J-1 visa compliance and international student and scholar support, ensuring adherence to federal regulations while delivering a high-quality student experience. The position also partners with the Director of Study Abroad to provide academic and advising support to students (both incoming and outgoing) participating in study abroad programs, including maintaining records of course equivalencies with exchange partners, supporting course registration, and promoting study abroad opportunities. This position will work closely with professional advising colleagues and faculty advisors across the schools and colleges to ensure student retention and graduation. Job Responsibilities Provide advising support to Mazzuchelli Honors Scholars including assisting with course selections, performing audits to check for graduation eligibility, supporting students transitioning into and out of the honors program, and following up with the Honors Director and University Registrar. Provide drop-in advising appointments for international and honors students; develop familiarity with the range of Dominican University academic programs to be able to accurately answer a broad range of student inquiries. Lead Federal Compliance & International Student Services - serve as a Designated School Official (DSO) and Alternate Responsible Officer (ARO) for SEVP, ensuring full institutional monitoring and compliance with all federal regulations governing F-1 (from pre-arrival through post-graduation, e.g. transfer, OPT, departure and after)  and J-1 students and scholars. This includes managing records in SEVIS, preparing and issuing I-20s to F-1 students, preparing and issuing DS-2019s for J-1 students and scholars, and managing the OPT process for international graduates. Act as the university’s subject matter expert on immigration policies, proactively interpreting regulatory changes and advising stakeholders. Comply with federal regulations, including appropriate record-keeping, to guide F-1 students through all stages of the international student life cycle. Evaluate and process Curricular Practical Training (CPT) applications for F-1 students. Review employer offer letters, job descriptions, and academic credit and alignment before updating form I-20 with CPT employment authorization. Drive Regulatory Awareness & Strategic Guidance - monitoring federal guidance and global developments impacting international students. Translate complex regulations into actionable guidance for students, faculty, and university leadership. Monitor and analyze updates in federal immigration regulations as it relates to F and J students and their dependent(s). Enhance International Student Experience - design, implement, and continuously improve a comprehensive international student orientation program. Maintain up-to-date resources and provide proactive support, including crisis response and referrals to appropriate campus services. Ensure seamless academic transitions for study abroad students – partner with the Director of Study Abroad regarding programs of study for incoming and outgoing exchange students; facilitate and monitor registration processes; provide assistance with adjustments to course registrations; maintain records of course equivalencies across partner institutions to support academic advising. Other related duties as assigned. Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree Two years (2) or more, relevant work experience in a higher education environment or combination of education and experience Previous experience with and knowledge of international student and exchange scholar populations and regulations, including understanding of SEVIS, F, and J visa requirements Position requires proof of US Citizenship or Permanent Residence required to serve as Designated School Official (DSO) and Alternate Responsible Officer (ARO), per Homeland Security Must pass periodic criminal background checks as required by federal regulations Strong organizational skills and attention to detail to maintain a high caseload of time-sensitive immigration requests Preferred Qualifications Experience with academic advising Experience working with a variety of academic information systems Experience studying, living, and/or working abroad Competencies Ability to interpret and apply complex policies and regulations Cultural awareness and the ability to work with a diverse student body Comfort with and capacity to work collaboratively within and across teams Exceptional attention to detail and data accuracy Strong communication skills and a high degree of professionalism Advanced proficiency in Microsoft Office (Excel, Word, Powerpoint) Demonstrated commitment to continuous professional development Strategic problem-solving and conflict resolution skills Capacity to work independently while contributing to team success Physical Demands: Ability to spend long durations of the workday sitting at a desk and working on a computer Ability to lift up to 15 pounds at times Note: accommodation will be made for applicants who cannot meet these physical demands Salary and FLSA Status Salary: $30.00/hour FLSA Status: Non-Exempt (hourly); Part-time 20-29 hours/week Benefits Professional development opportunities Tuition remission for employees and their dependents based on hours worked Generous paid time off (PTO) Employment at Dominican University is contingent upon the successful completion of a background investigation. About Dominican University Dominican University is a Catholic, comprehensive teaching university located in River Forest, a suburb of Chicago, with an additional campus in the Pilsen neighborhood of Chicago. Accredited by the Higher Learning Commission, Dominican University offers associate, baccalaureate, master’s, and doctoral degrees. It is highly regarded for its academic rigor, thoughtful accompaniment of students, intentional affordability, and values-based, relationship-centered learning environment. Dominican currently enrolls over 3,300 students, including 2,280 undergraduates and 1,027 graduate students. Sixty-eight percent (68%) of undergraduate students identify as Latinx, 5% as Black or African American, and 3% as Asian. Under-represented minority students comprise 77% of the undergraduate enrollment and 38% of the graduate enrollment. Over 90 percent of undergraduates receive some form of financial aid. Nearly half of all undergraduates are first-generation college students; over half are federal Pell Grant recipients, illustrating their families’ level of income; and 58% are eligible for low-income MAP grants from the State of Illinois. Recognized since 2011 as a Hispanic-Serving Institution (HSI) by the U.S. Department of Education, Dominican is committed to expanding and enhancing educational opportunities for Latinx students and all students from historically underrepresented groups. For more information, visit www.dom.edu. Expectations for all Dominican Employees: To support the University's mission of preparing students to pursue truth, give compassionate service, and participate in the creation of a more just and humane world, engage in university service work that promotes collaboration and community building. This includes participating in organizational initiatives, supporting campus events, contributing to community outreach, and fostering a diverse and inclusive environment through involvement in various staff-driven activities and groups. Institutional Statement Dominican University is committed to fostering a diverse and inclusive academic community. We encourage applications from individuals of all backgrounds. Upon request, reasonable accommodations in the application process will be provided to individuals with disabilities. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement Dominican University is an equal opportunity employer and encourages applications from women, Apply for this Position Go back to the job list powered by Dominican University | (708) 366-2490"
